+## How this changes the circulation inquiry
 
-## Version and circulation questions
+- **April review and onward routing.** The scan supplies evidence of Hyde engaging with a draft and of Farmer's stated plan to circulate it to the front office. The quoted conclusion is a new way to check candidate draft versions. The embedded email's destination is Hyde and the proposed onward destination is the front office. Preserve both beside the four staff members' later description of the April 6 memo as intended for commissioners and the front office and Marcus's differing recollection of the April 22 discussion. The scan supplies neither April 22 minutes nor the front office's acknowledgment. [Earlier circulation comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/5fe51e466b12474ae2f69d6e7f449b341d8bd6f0/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-referral-memo-distribution-2026-11-05/README.md)
+- **June version and scope.** The June 7 memo copies qualify the knowledge allegation and retain negligence as an alternative. The June 8 agenda describes a later distribution to commissioners. The Hyde binder cover cites June 9, while the June 9 notes record discussion. Each is a separate observation. The April reply supports an earlier review of a draft. It leaves the identity of the memo circulated or discussed in June open. [June 7 and June 9 date comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b85d1ee7708e975f53d037ab4284ba51b1348e9b/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-hyde-tab11-memo-crosswalk-2026-11-08/README.md) · [June 8 agenda comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0d9f2479de37c210734dec68b9b5d0ef96553302/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-june8-agenda-transmittal-2026-11-08/README.md)
+- **Interpretation.** This is contemporaneous correspondence about how to characterize staff evidence and whether to pursue purpose. It supports the existence of that evidentiary disagreement. Both the writer's characterization of deception and her assessment of its limits are preserved. The letter supplies no independent test of agency intent or evidence that her concerns resulted in withholding.
 
-- **Keep the date fields separate.** The Hyde Tab 5-13 cover cites a **June 9, 2004** memo in Tab 11, pp. 8–9. Hyde Tab 5-11 and the Hamilton copy visibly date the Zelikow–Farmer memo **June 7, 2004**. The newly acquired June 8 agenda gives a planned distribution day. The June 9 notes use the shorthand **Farmer Memo**. The June 8 agenda supplies the expected authors, audience, subject and day for a search, while the version actually sent remains unresolved. [Tab 11 comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b85d1ee7708e975f53d037ab4284ba51b1348e9b/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-hyde-tab11-memo-crosswalk-2026-11-08/README.md)
-- **Keep proposals, discussion and execution separate.** The agenda calls its times notional. The June 9 notes record a question about referral and remarks about notice and timing. Their physical p. 19 passage has no clock time, vote or distribution record. The agenda's future-tense sentence leaves actual sending and receipt open. The later referral letter and reported dispatch remain separate evidence. [Referral and enclosure comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/fed8cf28467343d943dee6c97bb09d46cd393b19/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-referral-enclosure-accounting-2026-11-08/README.md)
